# Fast Cursor executor | frontend

- **Implement, do not redesign.** Read the *one* selected `docs/changes/<name>/CHANGE.md`, its exact F-criterion if needed, and the 2–5 source anchors. Architecture (TanStack Query, RHF/Zod, Next SSR, typed mutation/receipts, SSE) is decided. Never autonomously select the next Change.
- Use the [pre-investigated source atlas](../../docs/engineering/frontend-execution-playbook.md#6-source-atlas-for-w01w21) **only for the current packet**. Avoid whole-repo searches, rereading old minutes, long plan transcripts, parallel research agents, new architecture or unnecessary web browsing. Escalate *specific* contradictions to ChatGPT/owner with evidence.
- **Fast feedback:** `pnpm` and filtered/direct workspace commands; keep warm Next/Vitest/TypeScript caches. Inspect `git diff --check` and editor diagnostics during edits. Use one targeted test at a logical boundary, targeted typecheck/lint after the Change, broad builds/E2E only at specified integration checkpoints. See [verification ladder](../../docs/engineering/frontend-execution-playbook.md#4-verification-ladder-stop-checking-every-keystroke).
- Never wipe `node_modules`/`.next`/`.turbo` or rerun install/build/CI without a concrete reason. `pnpm test:focus` drops disposable `offscreen_auth_test` and needs explicit safety permission. Never call game providers or run deployment automatically.
- Report **diff/paths, checks actually run, one normal + one negative case, material unresolved issue and next dependency** in a compact receipt. Do not claim cached output or a mocked test proves a live backend outcome.
